{% comment %}
  Renders the Purelane rating line: star glyph, value, review count.

  Reads the same metafields Dawn's own card already reads
  (snippets/card-product.liquid lines 173-206): reviews.rating and
  reviews.rating_count. Those are Shopify's standard review metafield
  definitions, so any review app that writes them works without changes.

  Two corrections to the prototype (reference line 1262):
  - The prototype prints five literal star glyphs regardless of the real value,
    and the value itself ("4.8") is typed into the markup. Here the value comes
    from the product and a single star marks the line.
  - The glyph carried the only meaning. Here the accessible text states the
    rating and the count in full.

  Renders nothing when the product has no rating, rather than showing "0".

  Accepts:
  - product: {Object} product to read metafields from (required)
  - show_count: {Boolean} include the review count. Default true (optional)

  Usage:
  {% render 'purelane-rating', product: card_product %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign rating = product.metafields.reviews.rating.value
  assign rating_count = product.metafields.reviews.rating_count.value
-%}

{%- if rating != blank and rating.rating != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign rating_value = rating.rating | round: 1
    assign rating_max = rating.scale_max | default: 5
  -%}
  <div class="pl-rating">
    <b class="pl-rating__value" aria-hidden="true">
      {%- render 'purelane-icon', icon: 'star' -%}
      {{ rating_value }}
    </b>
    {%- if show_count != false and rating_count != blank -%}
      <span aria-hidden="true">
        &middot; {{ rating_count }} {{ reviews_label | default: 'reviews' }}
      </span>
    {%- endif -%}
    <span class="pl-sr">
      {{- 'accessibility.star_reviews_info' | t: rating_value: rating_value, rating_max: rating_max -}}
      {%- if show_count != false and rating_count != blank -%}
        {{ ' ' }}{{ rating_count }} {{ 'accessibility.total_reviews' | t }}
      {%- endif -%}
    </span>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
